      <h2>About my work</h2>
      <p>My research focuses on the topology and quantum geometry of electronic band structures. I am especially interested in how the geometric information of noninteracting wave functions constrains what may happen when electrons interact.</p>
      <p>My work on quaternion-Kähler geometry of Kramers pairs provides a geometric framework for time-reversal-symmetric multiband states. I hope to explore how such structures can inform the study of correlated phases, without claiming that these phases have already been established by this approach.</p>
      <h2>Academic background</h2>
      <dl class="academic-facts">
        <div><dt>Current program</dt><dd>Integrated M.S./Ph.D. Program in Physics, Seoul National University</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Expected Ph.D. completion</dt><dd>August 2027</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Advisor</dt><dd>Prof. Bohm-Jung Yang</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <h2>Broader interests</h2>
      <p>Correlations in electronic bands, topological order, symmetry-protected topological phases, generalized symmetries, and the interplay between many-body physics and quantum geometry.</p>
